 { Once the endgame phase is reached, the king usually leaves the role of being an object of attack behind and becomes a great attacking piece himself. Moreover, with the number of pieces being reduced, his contributions to the battle will be essential for either side. Throughout the book we have seen many examples highlighting the importance of an active king in the endgame; e.g. Kramnik-Deep Fritz, Polugaevsky-Tal, Alekhine-Euwe and Ljubojevic-Gligoric, just to name a few. Moreover, the King first! section in Chapter One showed some related ideas. Here we examine a few further examples. }  
 *

